ble" class="Avatar Avatar--medium" as="div" href="https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/16915869-linda-they-got-the-mustard-out" tabindex="0"><img data-testid="image" class="Avatar__image" alt="Profile Image for Linda ~ they got the mustard out! ~." src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1473475487i/16915869._UX200_CR0,33,200,200_.jpg"/></a></section><section class="ReviewerProfile__info"><span class="Text Text__title4"><div data-testid="name" class="ReviewerProfile__name"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/16915869-linda-they-got-the-mustard-out">Linda ~ they got the mustard out! ~</a></div></span><span class="Text Text__body3 Text__subdued"><div class="ReviewerProfile__meta"><span>1,921 reviews</span><span><span>149 followers</span></span></div></span></section><div data-testid="follow" class="ReviewerProfile__follow"><div class="FollowButton"><div class="ToggleButton" data-testid="ToggleButton"><span class="ToggleButton__noHover"><div class="Button__container Button__container--block"><button type="button" class="Button Button--primary Button--medium Button--block" aria-label="Follow Linda ~ they got the mustard out! ~"><span class="Button__labelItem">Follow</span></button></div></span><span class="ToggleButton__hover"><div class="Button__container Button__container--block"><button type="button" class="Button Button--primary Button--medium Button--block" aria-label="Follow Linda ~ they got the mustard out! ~"><span class="Button__labelItem">Follow</span></button></div></span></div></div></div></div></div><section class="ReviewCard__content"><section class="ReviewCard__row"><div class="ShelfStatus"><b>Did Not Finish</b></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5176256181">December 24, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">DNF @ 29%<br /><br />Well, this book hangover has been brutal to the sacrifices, lol. MDZS/GMDC takes no prisoners. 🙈 But that's what sacrifices are for. 😂<br /><br />This started out promising, but quickly started going downhill. First, this is over 10,000 locations long and the first in a series of however many books, so the author has ample time to build up the relationship. Instead, she rushes them into bed before they barely know each other and despite various difficult obstacles that cause our supposedly intelligent MCs to act incredibly stupidly. I felt zero chemistry between them, since all they do is notice that the other is manly-man/gorgeous, and they don't really spend any time actually talking to each other. Four days in, one is already thinking he's in love and the other is making plans to take his new bf back home with him. *sigh*<br /><br />This is a standard fantasy world with magic users, dwarfs, elves and territorial disputes. There are no dwarfs or elves in this book though, at least not up to the point where I finally threw in the towel. The realm this takes place in is clearly coded after ancient Scotland. They don't trust magic users and sequester them away to learn healing but don't allow them out unless there's a war or plague. ... Okay. The queen's also a total no-homo in regards to her youngest son. Why? Because you can never have too many potential heirs, I guess. (There's an old history tale of the youngest son of the youngest son being the only survivor in a potential coup to carry on the line. So there's that.) She already had one previous ambassador exiled when he was caught with her son, political ramifications be damned, and she's got permanent sourpuss face over this new ambassador, who was stupid enough to kiss the prince in the middle of a pub. Despite being so paranoid about her son's clandestine activities, and despite him being a prince, he's wandering around without escort or attendants. The ambassador, who is also a prince, despite speaking/thinking often of his tutors on the ship ride over, comes ashore alone, without attendants or retinue. So I guess they're just chilling on the boat this whole time? Who needs to guard him or help him out with the cultural hurdles and language barriers (since he's a last-minute replacement and was getting a crash course on the journey over)? In a land that hates magic users, and a queen who hates gays, what is this gay, magic-flaunting ambassador to do? Pork her son at every opportunity possible, obviously. 🤦🏻‍♀️ (Oh, and he owns slaves, since slavery is a-ok in his empire. But they were gifts, and they're old, and he treats them like family, so it's ok, ok? Don't worry about it. He's a kind slave master. He didn't even bring any of his slaves with him, not wanting to risk their health on the journey. See? He's great! (Though if another review is correct, the reason behind why he insists on getting clear consent from Hamish is less than ideal and involved a slave.))<br /><br />My interest was flagging quickly, but I kept reading in hopes that it would finally start going somewhere with the plot, but they kept getting distracted by their loins.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/16915869?shelf=fantasy" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fantasy</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/16915869?shelf=lgbtq" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">lgbtq</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/16915869?shelf=m-m" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">m-m</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><